    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0171" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.333D3/7–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-07T15:00:00-03:00">July 7, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2430. Guedes now attempting to form group of nine large Santos exporters to carry
                    the understanding mentioned in Department’s 2048, July 3, 10 p.m. He states that
                    several of the firms have already promised to cooperate and pool resources, but
                    he does not expect to be able to give definite assurances until some time next
                    week.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile DNC moving average of 20,000 bags a day from its stocks at São Paulo to
                    Santos from which it can loan coffee to firms prepared to ship.</p>
                <p>Embassy will immediately report all further developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
